{"type":"npc","name":"Ceasg","folder":null,"system":{"attributes":{"hp":{"value":320,"temp":0,"max":320,"details":"life shell"},"ac":{"value":35,"details":""},"allSaves":{"value":""},"speed":{"value":10,"otherSpeeds":[],"details":""},"weaknesses":[{"type":"cold-iron","value":15,"exceptions":[]}]},"initiative":{"statistic":"perception"},"details":{"languages":{"value":["common","fey","thalassic"],"details":""},"level":{"value":14},"blurb":"","publicNotes":"<p>Ceasgs are large, aquatic fey related to nixies. While they sometimes trade with coastal villages, ceasgs distrust humanoids due to a history of being exploited for their magical abilities and are quick to assume they are being taken advantage of. If a ceasg feels offended, they may resort to swallowing hostages to ensure fair treatment. Ceasgs can be dangerous foes, as slaying them is not enough to stop their wrath. In a process superficially similar to lichdom, ceasgs store their souls in organic vessels and can't be killed unless their vessels are destroyed.</p><h2>Descendants of the Deep</h2><p>Though naturally distrustful of humanoids, ceasgs can't seem to help but hail sailors who ride their waves or travelers who journey along their shores. Ceasgs have even been known to fall in love with mortals. Such infatuations are usually short-lived, though occasionally they blossom into true romances that last until the mortal inevitably ages and dies. The offspring of these unions might exhibit the fey features of their ceasg parent or appear to be entirely mortal, apart from a supernatural proclivity for maritime endeavors. In either case, ceasgs can always sense the presence of their children or other descendants and will sometimes show them favor, guiding them through a raging storm or leading them to sunken treasure.</p><h2>Suggested Monster Parts</h2><p><strong>Monster Parts</strong> 560/1,250/2,300 gp</p><p><strong>Eligible Refinements</strong> weapons (bludgeoning, piercing), armor (light, medium), perception item, skill items (Acrobatics, Athletics, Deception, Diplomacy, Intimidation, Lore [Sailing], Nature, Performance, Stealth)</p><p><strong>Eligible Imbued Properties</strong> body, bane, charisma, dexterity, elongating, energy resistant (vitality), intelligence, sensory (darkvision), spells (Primal: @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.oUDNCArkQTdhllxD]{Aqueous Orb}, @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.vLA0q0WOK2YPuJs6]{Charm}, @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.zfn5RqAdF63neqpP]{Control Water}, @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.IxhGEKl63R4QBvkj]{Frostbite}, @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Y3G6Y6EDgCY0s3fq]{Hydraulic Torrent}, @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.MZGkMsPBztFN0pUO]{Water Breathing}), spiked, strength, water, wild</p>","privateNotes":"","publication":{"title":"Battlezoo Bestiary: Elemental Storm (Pathfinder)","authors":"Eli Burry-Schnepp","license":"ORC","remaster":true}},"resources":{},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":0.941,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"abilities":{"str":{"mod":8},"dex":{"mod":5},"con":{"mod":3},"int":{"mod":5},"wis":{"mod":4},"cha":{"mod":8}},"perception":{"details":"","mod":25,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision"}],"vision":true},"saves":{"fortitude":{"value":22,"saveDetail":""},"reflex":{"value":28,"saveDetail":""},"will":{"value":25,"saveDetail":""}},"skills":{"acrobatics":{"base":25},"athletics":{"base":28},"deception":{"base":26},"diplomacy":{"base":26},"intimidation":{"base":28},"nature":{"base":26},"performance":{"base":26},"stealth":{"base":25}},"traits":{"value":["amphibious","fey","water"],"rarity":"rare","size":{"value":"huge"}}},"_id":"DLmtdaeJCQFL8STN","img":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/portraits/ceasg.webp","prototypeToken":{"name":"Ceasg","displayName":0,"actorLink":false,"appendNumber":false,"prependAdjective":false,"width":3,"height":3,"texture":{"src":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/tokens/ceasg.webp","anchorX":0.5,"anchorY":0.5,"offsetX":0,"offsetY":0,"fit":"contain","scaleX":1,"scaleY":1,"rotation":0,"tint":"#ffffff","alphaThreshold":0.75},"lockRotation":false,"rotation":0,"alpha":1,"disposition":-1,"displayBars":0,"bar1":{"attribute":"attributes.hp"},"bar2":{"attribute":null},"light":{"negative":false,"priority":0,"alpha":0.5,"angle":360,"bright":0,"color":null,"coloration":1,"dim":0,"attenuation":0.5,"luminosity":0.5,"saturation":0,"contrast":0,"shadows":0,"animation":{"type":null,"speed":5,"intensity":5,"reverse":false},"darkness":{"min":0,"max":1}},"sight":{"enabled":false,"range":0,"angle":360,"visionMode":"basic","color":null,"attenuation":0.1,"brightness":0,"saturation":0,"contrast":0},"detectionModes":[],"occludable":{"radius":0},"ring":{"enabled":true,"colors":{"ring":null,"background":null},"effects":1,"subject":{"scale":1,"texture":"modules/battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e/assets/subjects/ceasg.webp"}},"flags":{"pf2e":{"linkToActorSize":true,"autoscale":false}},"randomImg":false,"turnMarker":{"mode":1,"animation":null,"src":null,"disposition":false},"movementAction":null},"items":[{"name":"Sailing Lore","type":"lore","system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":""},"rules":[],"slug":null,"_migration":{"version":0.942,"lastMigration":null,"previous":{"schema":0.941,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"traits":{"otherTags":[]},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"mod":{"value":24},"proficient":{"value":0}},"effects":[],"_id":"tVP4yWeTSpd1DYPD","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/lore.svg","folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"}},{"name":"Primal Innate Spells","type":"spellcastingEntry","system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":""},"rules":[],"slug":null,"_migration":{"version":0.942,"lastMigration":null},"traits":{"otherTags":[]},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"ability":{"value":"cha"},"spelldc":{"value":26,"dc":34},"tradition":{"value":"primal"},"prepared":{"value":"innate"},"showSlotlessLevels":{"value":false},"proficiency":{"value":1},"slots":{"slot0":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0},"slot1":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0},"slot2":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0},"slot3":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0},"slot4":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0},"slot5":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0},"slot6":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0},"slot7":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0},"slot8":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0},"slot9":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0},"slot10":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0},"slot11":{"prepared":[],"value":0,"max":0}},"autoHeightenLevel":{"value":null}},"_id":"E4qa1MTgLVAm5YfK","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/spellcastingEntry.svg","effects":[],"folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"}},{"folder":"7cyoYPoPYA01mErU","img":"icons/magic/air/wind-tornado-funnel-damage-blue.webp","name":"Hydraulic Torrent","system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>A swirling torrent of water manifests along a straight line, battering creatures and unattended objects in its path and possibly pushing them away from you. The torrent deals 8d6 bludgeoning damage. Each creature in the area must attempt a basic Fortitude save; unattended objects automatically fail. Creatures and objects that fail are also knocked back 5 feet (10 feet on a critical failure).</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Heightened (+1)</strong> The damage increases by 2d6.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":"hydraulic-torrent","_migration":{"version":0.942,"lastMigration":null,"previous":null},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["concentrate","manipulate","water"],"rarity":"common","traditions":["primal"]},"publication":{"title":"Pathfinder Player Core","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"level":{"value":4},"requirements":"","target":{"value":""},"range":{"value":""},"area":{"type":"line","value":60},"time":{"value":"2"},"duration":{"value":"","sustained":false},"damage":{"0":{"applyMod":false,"category":null,"formula":"8d6","kinds":["damage"],"materials":[],"type":"bludgeoning"}},"defense":{"save":{"basic":true,"statistic":"fortitude"}},"cost":{"value":""},"location":{"value":"E4qa1MTgLVAm5YfK","heightenedLevel":6,"uses":{"max":3,"value":3}},"counteraction":false,"heightening":{"area":0,"damage":{"0":"2d6"},"interval":1,"type":"interval"}},"type":"spell","_stats":{"compendiumSource":"Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.Y3G6Y6EDgCY0s3fq","duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"},"effects":[],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_id":"2F5MAPazhoYZmXoY"},{"folder":"iDjm2cXyRAe4VZ35","img":"icons/magic/fire/explosion-flame-blue.webp","name":"Control Water","system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>By imposing your will upon the water, you can raise or lower the level of water in the chosen area by 10 feet. Creatures that have the water trait and that are in the area when you Cast the Spell must attempt a Fortitude save, with the effects of the @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.WsUwpfmhKrKwoIe3]{Slow} spell.</p>\n<p><strong>Area</strong> 50 feet long by 50 feet wide</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":"control-water","_migration":{"version":0.942,"lastMigration":null,"previous":null},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["concentrate","manipulate","water"],"rarity":"common","traditions":["arcane","primal"]},"publication":{"title":"Pathfinder Player Core","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"level":{"value":5},"requirements":"","target":{"value":""},"range":{"value":"500 feet"},"area":null,"time":{"value":"2"},"duration":{"value":"1 hour","sustained":false},"damage":{},"defense":{"save":{"basic":false,"statistic":"fortitude"}},"cost":{"value":""},"location":{"value":"E4qa1MTgLVAm5YfK","heightenedLevel":5,"uses":{"max":3,"value":3}},"counteraction":false},"type":"spell","_stats":{"compendiumSource":"Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.zfn5RqAdF63neqpP","duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"},"effects":[],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_id":"e7LzHN1wTV4UCxSk"},{"folder":"T8AzYUgNIAgTJ9Iz","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/spells/charm.webp","name":"Charm","system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>To the target, your words are honey and your visage seems bathed in a dreamy haze. It must attempt a Will save, with a +4 circumstance bonus if you or your allies recently threatened it or used hostile actions against it.</p>\n<p>You can Dismiss the spell. If you use hostile actions against the target, the spell ends. When the spell ends, the target doesn't necessarily realize it was charmed unless its friendship with you or the actions you convinced it to take clash with its expectations, meaning you could potentially convince the target to continue being your friend via mundane means.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The target is unaffected and aware you tried to charm it.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The target is unaffected but thinks your spell was something harmless instead of charm, unless it identifies the spell.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The target's attitude becomes @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.v66R7FdOf11l94im]{Friendly} toward you. If it was Friendly, it becomes @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.v44P3WUcU1j0115l]{Helpful}. It can't use hostile actions against you.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The target's attitude becomes Helpful toward you, and it can't use hostile actions against you.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Heightened (4th)</strong> The duration lasts until the next time you make your daily preparations.</p>\n<p><strong>Heightened (8th)</strong> The duration lasts until the next time you make your daily preparations, and you can target up to 10 creatures.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":"charm","_migration":{"version":0.942,"lastMigration":null,"previous":null},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["concentrate","emotion","incapacitation","manipulate","mental","subtle"],"rarity":"common","traditions":["arcane","occult","primal"]},"publication":{"title":"Pathfinder Player Core","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"level":{"value":1},"requirements":"","target":{"value":"1 creature"},"range":{"value":"30 feet"},"area":null,"time":{"value":"2"},"duration":{"value":"1 hour","sustained":false},"damage":{},"defense":{"save":{"basic":false,"statistic":"will"}},"cost":{"value":""},"location":{"value":"E4qa1MTgLVAm5YfK","heightenedLevel":4,"uses":{"max":3,"value":3}},"counteraction":false,"heightening":{"levels":{"8":{"target":{"value":"10 creatures"}}},"type":"fixed"}},"type":"spell","_stats":{"compendiumSource":"Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.vLA0q0WOK2YPuJs6","duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"},"effects":[],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_id":"ZZuJjMrebGMg2BXN"},{"folder":"lPzcDrjGDFbzuF2r","img":"icons/magic/water/elemental-water.webp","name":"Water Breathing (At Will)","system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>The targets can breathe underwater.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Heightened (3rd)</strong> The duration increases to 8 hours.</p>\n<p><strong>Heightened (4th)</strong> The duration increases to until your next daily preparations.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":"water-breathing","_migration":{"version":0.942,"lastMigration":null,"previous":null},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["concentrate","manipulate","water"],"rarity":"common","traditions":["arcane","divine","primal"]},"publication":{"title":"Pathfinder Player Core","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"level":{"value":2},"requirements":"","target":{"value":"up to 5 creatures"},"range":{"value":"30 feet"},"area":null,"time":{"value":"1 minute"},"duration":{"value":"1 hour","sustained":false},"damage":{},"defense":null,"cost":{"value":""},"location":{"value":"E4qa1MTgLVAm5YfK","heightenedLevel":4},"counteraction":false},"type":"spell","_stats":{"compendiumSource":"Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.MZGkMsPBztFN0pUO","duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"},"effects":[],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_id":"hvaQePLOKA1L3lXQ"},{"folder":"4fJHnYFqH0VjZXPv","img":"icons/commodities/materials/slime-thick-blue.webp","name":"Aqueous Orb (At Will)","system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>A sphere of water 10 feet in diameter forms in an unoccupied space in range, either on the ground or on the surface of a liquid.</p>\n<p>When you Cast this Spell and each time you Sustain it, you can roll the orb, moving it up to 10 feet along the ground or the surface of a liquid.</p>\n<p>The orb can move through the spaces of any creatures or obstacles that wouldn't stop the flow of water. It extinguishes non-magical fires it moves through of its size or smaller, and it attempts to counteract any magical fires it moves through. If it fails to counteract a given fire, it can't counteract that fire for the duration of the spell.</p>\n<p>The orb can engulf Large or smaller creatures it moves through, and it can contain as many creatures as fit in its space. The orb can try to engulf the same creature only once per turn, even if you roll it onto a creature's space more than once. Any Large or smaller creature whose space the orb tries to move through can attempt a Reflex save.</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The creature can either let the orb pass (remaining in its space or moving out of the orb's path into a space of the creature's choice) or allow itself to be pushed in front of the orb to the end of the orb's movement.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is engulfed in the orb. It moves along with the orb and must hold its breath or begin suffocating (unless it can breathe in water). An engulfed Medium or smaller creature and anyone trying to affect that creature follow the normal rules for aquatic battles. An engulfed Large creature is usually big enough that parts of it stick out from the water, and it can reach out of the water. The creature can get free either by Swimming with a successful @Check[athletics|traits:action:swim|dc:10] check or by @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.SkZAQRkLLkmBQNB9]{Escaping} against your spell DC. A freed creature exits the orb's space and can immediately breathe.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, but the creature can't Swim to get free.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":"aqueous-orb","_migration":{"version":0.942,"lastMigration":null,"previous":null},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["concentrate","manipulate","water"],"rarity":"common","traditions":["arcane","primal"]},"publication":{"title":"Pathfinder Player Core","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"level":{"value":3},"requirements":"","target":{"value":""},"range":{"value":"60 feet"},"area":null,"time":{"value":"2"},"duration":{"value":"1 minute","sustained":true},"damage":{},"defense":{"save":{"basic":false,"statistic":"reflex"}},"cost":{"value":""},"location":{"value":"E4qa1MTgLVAm5YfK","heightenedLevel":3},"counteraction":true},"type":"spell","_stats":{"compendiumSource":"Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.oUDNCArkQTdhllxD","duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"},"effects":[],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_id":"EcxCEUqag2FOxqTe"},{"folder":"D7UVaOiB40wTR6kv","img":"icons/magic/movement/trail-streak-impact-blue.webp","name":"Frostbite","system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>An orb of biting cold coalesces around your target, freezing its body. The target takes 2d4 cold damage with a basic Fortitude save. On a critical failure, the target also gains weakness 1 to bludgeoning until the start of your next turn.</p>\n<p>@UUID[Compendium.pf2e.spell-effects.Item.DdqWMj7cuf4S1bgr]{Spell Effect: Frostbite}</p>\n<hr />\n<p><strong>Heightened (+1)</strong> The damage increases by 1d4 and the weakness on a critical failure increases by 1.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":"frostbite","_migration":{"version":0.942,"lastMigration":null,"previous":null},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["cantrip","cold","concentrate","manipulate"],"rarity":"common","traditions":["arcane","primal"]},"publication":{"title":"Pathfinder Player Core","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"level":{"value":1},"requirements":"","target":{"value":"1 creature"},"range":{"value":"60 feet"},"area":null,"time":{"value":"2"},"duration":{"value":"","sustained":false},"damage":{"3bsJUDEgedKhPx6T":{"applyMod":false,"category":null,"formula":"2d4","kinds":["damage"],"materials":[],"type":"cold"}},"defense":{"save":{"basic":true,"statistic":"fortitude"}},"cost":{"value":""},"location":{"value":"E4qa1MTgLVAm5YfK"},"counteraction":false,"heightening":{"damage":{"3bsJUDEgedKhPx6T":"1d4"},"interval":1,"type":"interval"}},"type":"spell","_stats":{"compendiumSource":"Compendium.pf2e.spells-srd.Item.IxhGEKl63R4QBvkj","duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"},"effects":[],"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_id":"Yt5pOMUQMr77CZgv"},{"type":"action","name":"Fascinated by Music","system":{"actionType":{"value":"passive"},"description":{"value":"<p>Musical performances can enthrall a ceasg, at least until the performer shows signs of hostility. A creature can attempt a Performance check to @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.EEDElIyin4z60PXx]{Perform} against the ceasg's Will DC.</p><hr /><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The ceasg is @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.AdPVz7rbaVSRxHFg]{Fascinated} by the performer for 1 minute.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The ceasg is fascinated by the performer for 3 rounds.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The ceasg is temporarily immune to the performer's attempts to fascinate them with a Performance for 1 hour.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, and the ceasg can use a reaction to Stride or Swim toward the performer. If this movement places the performer within their reach, they can make a jaws Strike.</p>","gm":""},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"rules":[],"slug":null,"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[]},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":null,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"actions":{"value":null},"category":"defensive","deathNote":false},"effects":[],"_id":"v5IFOKxTsqJDEW3z","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg","folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"}},{"type":"action","name":"Life Shell","system":{"actionType":{"value":"passive"},"description":{"value":"<p>The ceasg keeps their soul in a magical container made from a hollow piece of organic material such as an egg, seashell, or skull. The shell has Hardness 10 and 40 Hit Points. Destroying the shell deals @Damage[6d10[mental]] damage to the ceasg (@Check[will|dc:35|basic] save). If the ceasg is slain while the shell is intact, the ceasg and any creatures they have swallowed dissolve into water and reform at the location of the life shell in [[/gmr 1d8 #days]]{1d8 days}. A swallowed creature is not dead during this time and can't be restored to life.</p>","gm":""},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"rules":[],"slug":null,"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["primal"]},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":null,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"actions":{"value":null},"category":"defensive","deathNote":false},"effects":[],"_id":"7gTSXpKzVreO3NZO","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg","folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"}},{"type":"action","name":"Protect Hostage","system":{"actionType":{"value":"free"},"description":{"value":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within the ceasg's stomach is reduced to 0 Hit Points or would die of suffocation</p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> The creature is @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.fBnFDH2MTzgFijKf]{Unconscious} but not dying. It doesn't take further damage from the ceasg's Swallow Whole, and it doesn't need to breathe.</p>","gm":""},"publication":{"title":"","authors":"","license":"OGL","remaster":false},"rules":[],"slug":null,"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":[]},"_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":{"schema":null,"foundry":"13.347","system":"7.3.1"}},"actions":{"value":null},"category":"defensive","deathNote":false},"effects":[],"_id":"wVPKAedFYG5uXnRP","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg","folder":null,"sort":0,"ownership":{"default":0,"1Lps0mi7tMJnjtuv":3},"flags":{},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.347","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.4.2"}},{"img":"systems/pf2e/icons/actions/Reaction.webp","name":"Reactive Strike","system":{"actionType":{"value":"reaction"},"actions":{"value":null},"category":"defensive","description":{"value":"<p>@Localize[PF2E.NPC.Abilities.Glossary.ReactiveStrike]</p>","gm":""},"publication":{"license":"ORC","remaster":true,"title":"Pathfinder Monster Core","authors":""},"rules":[],"traits":{"value":[],"otherTags":[]},"slug":"reactive-strike","_migration":{"version":0.942,"previous":null}},"type":"action","_stats":{"c